  body: |
    # Employed earner in the ESA earnings source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes an employed earner as someone gainfully employed in Great Britain under a contract of service or in an office with general earnings, including specified office holders.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 49013–49015 are benefit-source definitions rather than a general employment-law status decision. The actual relationship, statutory versions, payment type and work continuing or ending remain separate questions.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 49013, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e6000e44a079b27f997f4e/dmg-Chap-49.pdf#page=5)
    - [DMG 49014, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e6000e44a079b27f997f4e/dmg-Chap-49.pdf#page=5)
    - [DMG 49015, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e6000e44a079b27f997f4e/dmg-Chap-49.pdf#page=5)
    - [DMG 49002, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e6000e44a079b27f997f4e/dmg-Chap-49.pdf#page=3)

